course: dictionary
lesson: 16019
title: A grassland word from Africa: veld
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A veld is a wide, open grassland with few trees. Picture a huge, flat space of grass with the sky reaching all the way round. «The farmer's cattle grazed across the veld all day.» Grazed means eating grass, and the wide space tells you the veld is a grassland.
explain: The word comes from southern Africa, especially South Africa. Context clues help here: «We drove for hours over the veld and saw no houses, only grass and sky.» Hours of driving with no houses and no trees tells you the veld is wide and empty.
explain: Some writers spell it veldt, as Rudyard Kipling did in his Just So Stories. Both spellings mean the same thing. When you meet a new word, look at the words around it, then swap your meaning into the sentence to check it still makes sense.
fact: Veld means wide, open grassland with few trees.
fact: The veld is mostly found in southern Africa, especially South Africa.
fact: The veld is a bit like the prairie in North America or the pampas in South America.
fact: Zebra, antelope and lions are animals that live on the veld.
fact: Kipling spelled it «veldt» in his Just So Stories, where the animals live on the High Veldt.
exercise: «The zebras ran across the veld, their stripes flashing in the sun.» What is the veld? | *A wide, open grassland with few trees | A busy city street | A deep, dark forest full of tall trees | A cold mountain covered in snow
exercise: «The lion watched the antelope from the tall grass of the veld.» What kind of place is the veld here? | A sandy beach by the sea | *An open grassland where animals live | A school playground | A frozen lake
exercise: Which word is another spelling of veld? | Vield | Wield | *Veldt | Velt
test: «Our school trip took us across the veld, where we saw antelope grazing far from any trees.» Where did the trip go? | A busy harbour by the sea | A tall, dark forest | *A wide grassland with few trees | A busy shopping centre
test: Which animal might you see on the veld? | A camel in the desert | *A zebra grazing in the grass | A penguin on the ice | A dolphin in the sea
exam: Which best describes the veld? | A deep valley covered in snow | A river that flows into the sea | A tiny village with many houses | *A wide, open grassland in southern Africa
